<title>USA: ContiFinancial sells $45.9 mln certificates.</title>
<headline>ContiFinancial sells $45.9 mln certificates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>ContiFinancial Corp said Tuesday it had closed the sale of $45.9 million of non-prime auto loan backed certificates issued by the Triad Auto Receivables Trust 1997-2.</p>
<p>The company said the deal was structured as a senior/subordinate issue consisting of three classes of fixed rate pass-through certificates. They were:</p>
<p>- 7.18 percent Asset Backed Certificates (Class A) with an initial aggregate principal balance of about $42.1 million</p>
<p>- 8.70 percent Asset Backed Certificates (Class B) with an initial aggregate principal balance of about $3.8 million</p>
<p>- 9.02 percent Asset Backed Certificates (Class C) with an initial aggregate principal balance of about $900,000.</p>
</text>
